182:## GB10 experiment and decision
184:**Hypothesis.** The six rules will derive the loop from the submitted source, without a function-name match or a hand-selected attention kernel. On a GB10, for each primary shape `(N,D)=(1024,64),(2048,64),(4096,64)`, the derived kernel will pass the above checks, use no global score/weight matrix, take at most **80% of unfused time** and at most **125% of hand-written streaming time**, and move fewer measured DRAM bytes than the unfused program. These thresholds are targets, not estimates from this worktree.
